# Programmatic SEO

**Intent:** Design SEO page programs at scale (templates + data) that rank without thin-content penalties. Not single-page optimization (`on-page-seo.mdc`), not site-wide diagnosis (`seo-audit.mdc`), not editorial blog strategy.

---

## Before you design **[core]**

1. Read `.agents/product-marketing.md` if present — ICP, conversion goal, category.
2. Answer the **fit gate** below honestly. If most gates fail, recommend a smaller editorial or on-page approach instead.

---

## Fit gate — is pSEO the right answer? **[core]**

pSEO works when **all** are true:

| Gate | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Real data | Structured source with depth (10+ fields/record ideal); not shallow scrape + AI filler |
| Volume | Aggregate long-tail demand exists; individual queries need not be huge |
| Queryable intent | User question answerable from structured data — not narrative judgment |
| Refresh budget | Update cadence matches query volatility (listings daily vs "best X 2026" annually) |
| QC capacity | Team can sample-audit, fix failures, and maintain quality as set grows |

**Probably not pSEO when:** shallow data, illusory keyword lists nobody searches, no QC budget, scaling AI thin pages without unique data.

---

## Data moat hierarchy **[core]**

| Rank | Source | Defensibility |
|------|--------|---------------|
| 1 | Proprietary / first-party | You created it; competitors can't copy |
| 2 | Product-derived | From your users/transactions |
| 3 | User-generated | Community reviews, submissions |
| 4 | Licensed | Exclusive or integrated feeds |
| 5 | Public / scraped | Weakest — easy to copy; thin-content risk |

**Moat test:** Could a competitor replicate your data source in 90 days? If yes, pSEO has no lasting edge.

---

## Core principles **[core]**

1. **Unique value per page** — not swapped city names in identical prose.
2. **Subfolders, not subdomains** — `yoursite.com/templates/resume/` not `templates.yoursite.com`.
3. **Genuine intent match** — page answers what people actually search.
4. **Quality over quantity** — 100 great pages beat 10,000 thin ones.
5. **Avoid penalties** — no doorway pages, keyword stuffing, duplicate clusters.

---

## 12 playbooks **[core]**

| Playbook | Pattern | Example |
|----------|---------|---------|
| Templates | `[type] template` | resume template |
| Curation | `best [category]` | best website builders |
| Conversions | `[X] to [Y]` | $10 USD to GBP |
| Comparisons | `[X] vs [Y]` | webflow vs wordpress |
| Examples | `[type] examples` | landing page examples |
| Locations | `[service] in [location]` | dentists in austin |
| Personas | `[product] for [audience]` | crm for real estate |
| Integrations | `[A] [B] integration` | slack asana integration |
| Glossary | `what is [term]` | what is pSEO |
| Translations | Localized content | multi-language sets |
| Directory | `[category] tools` | ai copywriting tools |
| Profiles | `[entity name]` | company or person profile |

**Choosing:**

| If you have… | Consider… |
|--------------|-----------|
| Proprietary data | Directory, Profiles |
| Many integrations | Integrations |
| Multi-segment audience | Personas |
| Local presence | Locations |
| Tool/utility product | Conversions |
| Expertise content | Glossary, Curation |
| Competitor landscape | Comparisons |

Layer playbooks when natural (e.g. "Best coworking spaces in San Diego").

