## Implementation framework **[core]**

### 1. Keyword pattern research
- Repeating structure + variables + combinatorial count
- Validate aggregate volume and trend; head vs long-tail distribution

### 2. Data requirements
- Fields per record; required vs optional; computed fields; cross-record links for internal linking
- Update-frequency tags (static vs volatile fields)

### 3. Template design
- **Above-the-fold answer** in first ~200 words (human + extractable)
- **Variable density** — graceful fallbacks for sparse records; progressive disclosure for dense
- **Heading hierarchy** maps to data sections, not decoration
- **Schema in template** — JSON-LD at scale per page type
- **Internal link slots** — 5–15 related/parent/sibling links per page
- Unique title + meta per URL

### 4. Internal linking
- Hub-and-spoke: category hub → spokes → cross-links
- No orphan pages; breadcrumbs + sitemap; keyword → canonical URL table

### 5. Indexation strategy
- Prioritize high-volume patterns first
- `noindex` very thin variations
- Separate sitemaps by page type when large
- Manage crawl budget on 500+ page sets

---

## Quality control **[core]**

### Pre-launch checklist

- [ ] Random sample page answers query competently in isolation
- [ ] Unique value vs parent/sibling pages
- [ ] Unique titles, metas, H1s
- [ ] Schema validates (Rich Results Test)
- [ ] Connected in site architecture; no orphans
- [ ] In XML sitemap; crawlable; no conflicting noindex

### Post-launch monitoring

Track: indexation rate, rankings, traffic, engagement, conversion.

Watch: thin-content warnings, ranking drops, manual actions, crawl errors.

Define metrics and review cadence **before** launch.

---

## Common mistakes **[core]**

- Thin templates (city/name swap only)
- Keyword cannibalization across generated URLs
- Over-generation with no search demand
- Stale or wrong data
- Pages built for crawlers, not users

---

## Output formats **[core]**

**Opportunity analysis** — table: pattern | est. pages | aggregate volume | data source | difficulty

**Strategy doc** — playbook choice, implementation plan, content uniqueness rules

**Page template spec** — URL pattern, title/meta templates, content blocks, schema type, linking rules

**Pre-launch checklist** — checkboxes as above

